# Intentional dev bypasses in the BDR Coverage Planner

Several stages in this app are short-circuited on purpose so UI work can
happen without a live robot. Do **not** remove these as "cleanup." They are
tracked in `docs/DEV_BYPASSES.md`.

When editing any of the files matched by this rule:

- If you are about to delete, disable, or refactor away one of the bypasses
  **without the user explicitly asking for it**, stop and surface the
  checklist entry in `docs/DEV_BYPASSES.md` instead.
- If the user asks to rewire a stage, update `docs/DEV_BYPASSES.md` (tick
  the box) in the same change.
- If you introduce a new temporary short-circuit, tag it with
  `// BDR_REWIRE: <short note>` and add a matching bullet to
  `docs/DEV_BYPASSES.md`.

Known bypass sites:

- `setup_screen.cpp` — dev bypass in `submit()`; hardcoded ping target.
- `startup_screen.cpp` — `kEnableLaunchDashboardPassthrough = true`.
- `app_shell.cpp` — `DashboardScreen::viewRecordingsRequested` intentionally
  unconnected.
- `planner_screen.cpp` — `nextStageRequested` has no emitter/receiver; no
  waypoint publish / autonomy handoff yet.
- `dashboard_screen.cpp` — info-card values are placeholders.

Before any "prepare for release" task, run:

```bash
rg -n 'BDR_REWIRE|Dev bypass|dev bypass|kEnable.*Passthrough' cpp/
```
